{
 "schema_version": 4,
 "description": "Strength standards per exercise. anchors = scaled e1RM at the beginner, novice, intermediate, advanced and elite levels, as a multiple of the reference bodyweight. Loads are scaled allometrically: scaled ratio = e1RM / (reference_bodyweight x (bodyweight / reference_bodyweight) ^ exponent), so a heavier lifter isn't penalised for not lifting in proportion to bodyweight. Bodyweight-kind lifts (e1RM includes bodyweight) use plain e1RM / bodyweight. Every non-bodyweight standard is base compound anchors x factor (the typical ratio of that exercise to the compound), so a typical lifter ranks about the same on both. Machine and cable anchors are multiplied by machine_strictness. Tier entry points: Iron 0, Bronze = beginner, Silver = novice, Gold = midpoint novice-intermediate, Platinum = intermediate, Emerald = midpoint intermediate-advanced, Diamond = advanced, Master = elite, Grandmaster = elite x 1.15, Challenger = elite x 1.30. per_hand: per dumbbell or per side. Source: tool/standards/exercise_data.py.",
